WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.562
Out in the field, the signal comes and goes.

00:00:03.682 --> 00:00:09.130
In this video you will save a measurement with
no signal at all, watch it wait on your phone,

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:13.402
and see OurWater send it by itself when the
signal returns.

00:00:14.217 --> 00:00:17.457
Out in the field, signal comes and goes.

00:00:17.577 --> 00:00:19.761
OurWater is ready for that.

00:00:19.881 --> 00:00:22.953
Start with Add a measurement, in the menu.

00:00:23.783 --> 00:00:26.519
The form starts with a Station box.

00:00:26.639 --> 00:00:30.167
Choose your station now, while you still have
signal.

00:00:30.287 --> 00:00:33.431
The station list needs the internet to load.

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:37.490
Type a few letters of its name, then click it.

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:41.330
From here on, the form works with no signal at
all.

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:44.358
Now we walk out of range.

00:00:44.478 --> 00:00:47.526
A message appears: You are offline.

00:00:47.646 --> 00:00:52.206
Measurements you save are kept on this device
and upload when you have signal.

00:00:53.017 --> 00:00:55.897
The date and time are already filled in.

00:00:56.017 --> 00:01:00.961
They are saved with your measurement, so later
it still shows when you really measured.

00:01:01.783 --> 00:01:05.407
Type the depth to water in metres, as usual.

00:01:05.527 --> 00:01:08.767
Here the water is twelve point four metres
down.

00:01:09.583 --> 00:01:12.847
Photos and videos need signal to upload.

00:01:12.967 --> 00:01:19.111
If you add one now, your numbers are still saved,
and OurWater tells you the picture was left out.

00:01:19.917 --> 00:01:22.101
Now click Save measurement.

00:01:22.221 --> 00:01:26.157
You do not wait for signal, and there is
nothing else to do.

00:01:26.983 --> 00:01:30.199
OurWater says: Saved on this device.

00:01:30.319 --> 00:01:33.415
It will upload by itself when you have signal.

00:01:33.535 --> 00:01:36.439
Your measurement is safe on your computer.

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:40.874
Click Close, and look at My measurements in
the menu.

00:01:40.994 --> 00:01:44.930
The small number shows how many measurements
are waiting to upload.

00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:46.922
Now it is one.

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:50.366
On My measurements, near the top,

00:01:50.486 --> 00:01:56.342
a box called Waiting to upload shows what is still
on your computer: the station, the value,

00:01:56.462 --> 00:01:58.334
and the time.

00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:03.974
Retry now sends the waiting measurements
straight away, if you have signal.

00:02:04.783 --> 00:02:08.095
Delete throws one away, after you confirm.

00:02:08.215 --> 00:02:11.767
A measurement that has not uploaded cannot be
brought back.

00:02:12.583 --> 00:02:14.743
Now the signal returns.

00:02:14.863 --> 00:02:16.735
You do nothing.

00:02:16.855 --> 00:02:22.327
OurWater sends your measurement by itself, and
says: All measurements uploaded.

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:27.542
The number beside My measurements has gone,
and so has the box.

00:02:27.662 --> 00:02:29.918
Nothing is waiting any more.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:34.590
And here is your measurement on the list, like
any other.

00:02:35.417 --> 00:02:37.289
One more case.

00:02:37.409 --> 00:02:40.649
Sometimes the server cannot accept a
measurement,

00:02:40.769 --> 00:02:44.585
for example if the station was removed while
you were away.

00:02:44.705 --> 00:02:46.577
Let us see.

00:02:47.383 --> 00:02:52.039
We go out of signal again, type thirteen point
one, and save.

00:02:52.159 --> 00:02:55.783
The same message appears: Saved on this
device.

00:02:56.617 --> 00:03:00.649
The signal returns, but this time the server
refuses it.

00:03:00.769 --> 00:03:04.777
OurWater tells you: Some measurements could
not be uploaded.

00:03:04.897 --> 00:03:07.249
Open My measurements to see them.

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:10.234
The measurement is not lost.

00:03:10.354 --> 00:03:16.882
It stays on your computer, in a box called Refused
measurements, and OurWater will not send it again.

00:03:17.683 --> 00:03:20.515
When you have read it, you can delete it.

00:03:20.635 --> 00:03:23.179
OurWater asks you to confirm.

00:03:23.299 --> 00:03:25.171
Click Delete.

00:03:25.983 --> 00:03:29.463
It is gone, and the message at the top has
cleared.

00:03:30.283 --> 00:03:32.155
Here is the tip.

00:03:32.275 --> 00:03:35.707
You never need to wait for signal to record a
measurement.

00:03:35.827 --> 00:03:40.291
Choose your station while you have signal,
then save wherever you are.

00:03:41.117 --> 00:03:46.301
Anything waiting is sent the next time
OurWater is open and your computer has signal.

00:03:46.421 --> 00:03:51.125
When the number beside My measurements
disappears, everything has been sent.

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:54.638
That is how to record with no signal.

00:03:54.758 --> 00:04:00.614
Choose your station while you can, save wherever you
are, and let OurWater send it later.

00:04:00.734 --> 00:04:03.614
Thank you for helping look after our water.
